        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Lands Battlefield, Culfadda, Ballymote, Co. Sligo, \r\nc. 7.40ha - c. 18.28 acres\r\n\r\nFor Sale by Live Virtual Online & Public Auction\r\n\r\nWednesday 28th of October 2026 \r\n\r\nAt\r\n\r\nWilsons Auctions, Kingswood Interchange, Naas Road, Dublin 22\r\n\r\nExcellent Potential \r\n\r\nLocation Ballymote.13km, Gorteen 7km, Boyle 12km, Sligo 36km. \r\n\r\nThe lands are located off a minor road accessed from the R294 7km south of Gurteen village and 13km south of Ballymote. Population (2022) 1,711. Ballymote is a historic market town located in Southern Co Sligo, in northwest Ireland, 20 km south of Sligo town. It is served by the Iarnród Éireann Dublin to Sligo train line. There are a selection of shops and services, pubs, schools and sporting clubs, there are factories just outside the town at Ballybrennan, and a small business park at Carrownanty on the R296 Road to Tobercurry The wider area is mainly agricultural, with many people commuting to Carrick on Shannon and Sligo town for work, where further amenities and transport links can be found. \r\n\r\nDescription Folio SL612\r\n\r\nThe lands are contained within folio SL612 and amount to c. 7.40ha - c. 18.28 acres. The subject lands are in two irregular shaped blocks in close proximity. They are laid out in large open plan manageable divisions, with mature boundaries of hedging and trees. The lands currently in grass of mixed quality suited to livestock and most farming enterprises. The lands are on an elevated site and have outstanding views of the verdant Sligo countryside. \r\n\r\nIdeal location for a one-off house, subject to the necessary planning. \r\n\r\nThe lands are being sold as seen and not subject to planning. \r\n\r\nCoordinates 54.016878, -8.440327\r\n\r\nViewing By Appointment Only\r\n\r\nSolicitor Iseult Cody, Beauchamps, Sir John Rogerson's Quay, Dublin 2 \r\n\r\nVAT Refer to legal contracts."
      },
